04:05:37.560 --> 04:05:38.880
You know, Wade, a few years ago,

04:05:39.020 --> 04:05:40.880
most observers would have named you

04:05:40.880 --> 04:05:43.240
a less than average defensive third baseman.

04:05:43.380 --> 04:05:45.800
Everybody talks about the three batting titles,

04:05:45.840 --> 04:05:47.760
but you've worked to become effective with the glove.

04:05:47.880 --> 04:05:48.400
Most definitely.

04:05:48.540 --> 04:05:50.760
I come out every day and work 15, 20 minutes extra

04:05:50.760 --> 04:05:52.360
on the ground balls.

04:05:52.660 --> 04:05:54.500
The fielding doesn't come easy,

04:05:54.520 --> 04:05:57.120
and I have to work a lot harder on my fielding

04:05:57.120 --> 04:05:58.960
than I do my hitting, and it's paying off.

04:05:59.460 --> 04:05:59.960
You made a...

04:06:00.000 --> 04:06:04.100
play on Mookie Wilson in the seventh last night. We're looking at a couple of the plays you turned

04:06:04.100 --> 04:06:08.640
in tonight, but in the seventh to take a hit away, and that preserved the 1-0 lead for Bruce Hurst

04:06:08.640 --> 04:06:12.580
last night at at least three fine plays tonight. Well, I didn't get any hits last night, but I felt

04:06:12.580 --> 04:06:18.100
like I went 4-4 with that diving play that I made that eventually saved the tying run, and the only

04:06:18.100 --> 04:06:21.900
way you can do it is contribute in games like this, and I'm just going out there trying to do the best

04:06:21.900 --> 04:06:26.820
I can. When people look at a guy with a lifetime batting average of .352 in three batting titles,

04:06:26.820 --> 04:06:29.960
They figure it's been a success story throughout, and yet just a few years.

04:06:30.000 --> 04:06:34.800
ago the Red Sox organization left you unprotected. Any team in baseball could

04:06:34.800 --> 04:06:38.420
have had you for 25 grand and they all passed. Well I'm glad they did because

04:06:38.420 --> 04:06:42.410
my heart's in Boston and I'm just doing all I can to contribute in this World

04:06:42.410 --> 04:06:46.780
Series. You guys have won five in a row after coming back from the brink of

04:06:46.780 --> 04:06:50.400
elimination down 3-1 and now you're up 2-0 heading back to Fenway. Got to be a

04:06:50.400 --> 04:06:53.260
great feeling. It's a great feeling. This team's got a lot of heart. They've

04:06:53.260 --> 04:06:56.540
never given up all year. We've had a lot of adversity on the field and off the

04:06:56.540 --> 04:06:59.690
field and we just put forth the effort.

04:07:00.540 --> 04:07:01.200
Thanks, Wade.

04:07:01.360 --> 04:07:04.620
The other side of the emotional scale embodied by Gary Carter.

04:07:04.800 --> 04:07:06.880
He's on the other side of the field with Marv Albert.

04:07:07.020 --> 04:07:07.200
Marv.

04:07:07.510 --> 04:07:08.290
All right, Bob.

04:07:08.450 --> 04:07:12.010
And for Gary Carter and the Mets, not a pleasant weekend here in New York.

04:07:12.170 --> 04:07:16.810
The scenario now, the worst possible case, you go to Fenway down two games to nothing.

04:07:17.110 --> 04:07:18.770
Well, it's going to be a tough goal, Marv.

04:07:18.930 --> 04:07:23.610
This Boston ball club, they got a great lineup, and they've gotten some good pitching performances.

04:07:23.610 --> 04:07:26.110
They got one tonight out of their bullpen, that's for sure.

04:07:26.290 --> 04:07:29.090
So, hey, we'll go on to Fenway, and hopefully we can pick it back up again.

04:07:29.090 --> 04:07:29.970
And that's still.

04:07:30.000 --> 04:07:32.780
Still not hitting. Is the ball club pressing at this point?

04:07:33.170 --> 04:07:36.910
I don't think so. We just came off one of the most pressurized series that we've ever played,

04:07:36.950 --> 04:07:40.710
and I don't know. You know, we got something going a little bit tonight, eight hits,

04:07:40.790 --> 04:07:43.130
but we'll have to pick it back up in Boston.

04:07:43.410 --> 04:07:46.210
Of course, out of the eight hits, two were bunt singles.

04:07:46.450 --> 04:07:49.150
Are you embarrassed by what has taken place here at Shea?

04:07:49.310 --> 04:07:53.370
No, not at all. I'm very proud of this ball club, and I think we've done it all year,

04:07:53.470 --> 04:07:57.290
and it's just a shame that, you know, these first two games went the way they did,

04:07:57.290 --> 04:07:59.900
But, you know, the Kansas City.

04:08:00.000 --> 04:08:03.360
The Royals were down two games last year and came back, so anything can happen.

04:08:03.460 --> 04:08:07.180
In fact, the Royals, the only club in World Series history to win

04:08:07.180 --> 04:08:10.260
after trailing two games to nothing, losing the first two at home.

04:08:10.560 --> 04:08:11.320
Exactly, Marv.

04:08:11.340 --> 04:08:14.720
That's just it about a World Series game and going on to Boston,

04:08:14.860 --> 04:08:16.420
and we feel like we can pick it back up again.

04:08:16.520 --> 04:08:19.060
All right, what about the pitching rotation Fernandez used tonight?

04:08:19.120 --> 04:08:21.460
It was thought that he would not pitch.

04:08:21.852 --> 04:08:26.252
In game number four at Fenway, the thought was Ricky Aguilera who was utilized tonight.

04:08:26.332 --> 04:08:27.872
Will it be darling on three days rest?

04:08:28.220 --> 04:08:30.000
Well, it could be, but I think that

04:08:30.000 --> 04:08:37.400
Davey is just using everybody he possibly can, and I would say, if anything, it might come back with Sid Fernandez.

04:08:37.932 --> 04:08:39.572
All right, Gary Carter of the Mets.

04:08:39.672 --> 04:08:40.912
Let's get back to Vin and Joe.

04:08:43.084 --> 04:08:43.344
Well, thanks.

04:08:43.344 --> 04:08:43.904
Thank you, fellas.

04:08:44.244 --> 04:08:48.924
And it's pretty easy for Wade Boggs on the ecstasy roll to be on the show.

04:08:49.084 --> 04:08:50.564
And our thanks to Gary Carter.

04:08:50.704 --> 04:08:53.444
I know he had to bite the bullet every second he was talking to Marv Aldridge.

04:08:53.724 --> 04:08:54.904
He's a class guy, then.

04:08:55.224 --> 04:08:58.644
You know, it hurts more to lose, and it feels good to win.

04:08:58.784 --> 04:08:59.244
You betcha.

04:08:59.344 --> 04:08:59.864
Well, remember.

04:09:00.124 --> 04:09:04.784
Tuesday, the World Series continues with Game 3, 8 p.m. Eastern time

04:09:04.784 --> 04:09:09.004
from Fenway Park in Boston on your World Series network, NBC.

04:09:09.584 --> 04:09:13.544
It'll be Bobby Ojeda, What a Story, the former Boston Red Sox.

04:09:13.820 --> 04:09:19.140
comes back with an 18-5 record against Dennis Oil Can Boyd,

04:09:19.180 --> 04:09:22.780
a youngster who was emotionally upset at the all-star time,

04:09:23.140 --> 04:09:26.980
suspended, returned, and now trying to make it six straight for Boston.

04:09:27.360 --> 04:09:29.720
The Mets will be fighting for their baseball lives.

04:09:30.000 --> 04:09:30.500
Join us then.

04:09:30.840 --> 04:09:32.340
Till then, for Joe Garagiola,

04:09:32.640 --> 04:09:34.580
Vin Scully wishing you a pleasant good evening.

04:09:35.660 --> 04:09:38.740
Promotional fee has been paid to NBC by United Airlines.

04:09:39.120 --> 04:09:41.540
Serving 13 cities in Asia and the Pacific.

04:09:41.880 --> 04:09:44.140
United, a fresh breeze across the Pacific.

04:09:46.604 --> 04:09:49.064
This has been a presentation of NBC Sports.

04:09:49.740 --> 04:09:53.200
Proud to be the network of the 1988 Summer Olympic Games.
